{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040275-the-paths-through-the-lie","id":1040275,"title":"The paths through the Lie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T16:24:06-08:00","id":1040275,"title":"The paths through the Lie","content":"I've always loved the way the Mastigos path description talks about seeing through the lie of distance when it explains that path, but the other paths don't seem to get that specific on which parts of the Lie they see through. What you would call the lies that the other paths see through? I could possibly see Acanthus as seeing through the lie of coincidence. What do you think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:25:23-08:00","id":1040529,"title":"","content":"It says so quite directly in the book (2e at least) when it talks about awakenings. It's on p60 in the book. But in my own words.<br /> <br /> Acanthus: Your actions don't matter, everything is predetermined and your life is tossed around by influences beyond your control.<br /> Mastigos: The illusion of distance, both physical and emotional. The idea that we should errect barriers between people through adhering to social norm and expected behavioural patterns.<br /> Moros: Nothing ever changes. After Death there is only oblivion.<br /> Obrimos: Humans are small and utterly helpless things in a very big, very scary universe.<br /> Thyrsus: Humans are more significant than mere animals and they can be exploited in whatever form we choose. There is nothing more to animals and base matter than it's raw components. We ARE the sum of our parts.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:27:58-08:00","id":1040531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040275-the-paths-through-the-lie?p=1040529#post1040529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says so quite directly in the book (2e at least) when it talks about awakenings. It's on p60 in the book. But in my own words.<br /> <br /> Acanthus: Your actions don't matter, everything is predetermined and your life is tossed around by influences beyond your control.<br /> Mastigos: The illusion of distance, both physical and emotional. The idea that we should errect barriers between people through adhering to social norm and expected behavioural patterns.<br /> Moros: Nothing ever changes. After Death there is only oblivion.<br /> Obrimos: Humans are small and utterly helpless things in a very big, very scary universe.<br /> Thyrsus: Humans are more significant than mere animals and they can be exploited in whatever form we choose. There is nothing more to animals and base matter than it's raw components. We ARE the sum of our parts.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Consequently, this is exactly what the Exarchs and the Seers who worship them represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:50:56-08:00","id":1043787,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> but I'd quibble on nuance for the Moros and Obrimos ones.<br /> <br /> Here's my take. A Path names the Lie, and then finds a specific way through it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979372-what-does-it-mean-to-walk-a-path-interpretations#post979372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acanthus<br /> The Acanthus is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>agency</b>. Everyone lives a scripted life, walking through the motions as actors on a stage. That\u2019s the story that the world tells, and you\u2019re just a face in that crowd, looking busy, lacking meaning. The Acanthus take control of the narrative, and thereby power over their life and the consequent world around them. They diverge from the script and say, \u201cYes, I can. And I will <i>because </i>I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mastigos<br /> The Mastigos is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>relationships</b>. Everyone lies to each other, putting up outward facades while their inner life is in turmoil. They turn away from each other and themselves, refusing to acknowledge necessary truths, poisoning their community. The Mastigos say that, \u201cDistance is a Lie.\u201d They forcibly create bridges where there were walls, and relish in the growing pains that come with having to come face-to-face with both others and oneself.<br /> <br /> Moros<br /> The Moros is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>components</b>. Everyone has a fixed notion of what constitutes an object, that lead is lead and gold is gold, that a child is a child and a man is a man. They go through their lives trying to acquire new things, ignoring that they could patch together everything they need from what they already have. The Moros breaks free of this attitude, reducing complexities into simple construction blocks and rebuilding them into something greater than the original arrangements. They watch and guide the transition from youth to age, from desolation to creation, from past to future.<br /> <br /> Obrimos<br /> The Obrimos is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>keystones</b>. Everyone presumes that things are disparate and disconnected, that you can manipulate one thing without affecting anything else. That\u2019s what it looks like on the outside: the superficial facade that people see everyday. The Obrimos understands that beneath such illusions is the hard truth of energy cycling through systems underlying the reality. They find the key that binds a thousand worlds together and turn it, opening a thousand locks at once and freeing a thousand minds with a single word, \u201cSee.\u201d<br /> <br /> Thyrsus<br /> The Thyrsus is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>negotiations</b>. Everyone sees an inanimate world, a terra nullius uncultivated and ripe for the taking. They can\u2019t see that something was already there, something that deserves consideration and comprehension. The Thyrsus hears these indigenous voices, speaks on their behalf, and answers them in return. The worlds are full of their own peoples, and those peoples must be accounted for when you endeavor their lands in your own right. It doesn\u2019t matter that a world might be within a person, or beyond a veil.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}